{
  "id": "COMPOUND:24757 - PROTEIN:5003",
  "verbalization": "Chaetochromin A is implicated in the regulation of ME-180 through a series of interconnected targets, all of which are involved in signaling pathways that modulate cellular responses. The evidence suggests that Chaetochromin A acts as a target for multiple compounds, ultimately leading to the activation or inhibition of ME-180. This pathway involves the mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 7 (MAP3K7), which is targeted by (4S)-tetradecan-4-ol and Methyl octadec-9-EN-12-ynoate, both of which are themselves targets of Chaetochromin A. Masonine, another compound targeted by Chaetochromin A, also leads to ME-180 activation. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Chaetochromin A influences ME-180, likely through the modulation of MAPK signaling. The consistent presence of these targets across different pathways supports a mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction between Chaetochromin A and the downstream targets remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence is robust and aligns with the expected role of Chaetochromin A in modulating cellular processes, making it a plausible candidate for a therapeutic relationship with ME-180.",
